  "scope": "Exact prewarm/session-loop/connection-shutdown Tokio task custody; early refresh admission close and active-permit wait; immutable typed cleanup error propagation; retained removed-session ownership and protected destructive archive/revert flows.",
  "adoption": "Apply combined-upper-02.patch only after current root gate terminal and review. Equivalent to preserved OWNERSHIP/PROPAGATION, both02 overlays, and test-only ownership03 lint corrections. Root binds full candidate source/tree and runs required gates. Lower transport separate.",
  "callsite_mapping": [
    "Session.start and prewarm reserve RetainedTask before spawning; cancelling observers never takes primary handle.",
    "handlers.shutdown_session_runtime closes refresh before teardown, joins prewarm, waits existing permit, observes current MCP shutdown task, still runs subsequent cleanup.",
    "SessionIo.shutdown_and_wait maps retained session outcome to CodexErr::ShutdownFailed; suspension and partial-startup cleanup observe it.",
    "ThreadManager snapshots live plus removed exact owners; failure IDs remain sticky; successful exact owners retire outside registry locks.",
    "AppServer distinguishes submit failure, known shutdown failure and timeout; timed-out observation stays pending. Destructive thread removal waits clean typed shutdown and pointer identity.",
    "connectors list propagates MCP shutdown-task failure with existing anyhow result.",
    "Internal ShutdownFailed maps existing InternalServerError wire category and is nonretryable; no schema/API wire variant."
  ],
