  "tests": "20 new behavioral tests across primitive/refresh/connection/session/manager/protocol/AS plus existing test adaptations. None executed. These are scoped unit/production-helper tests; real core/AppServer held MCP integration and process-final acceptance remain required.",
  "dependency_changes": "None in this upper proposal; existing async-utils edges already present.",
  "known_limits": [
    "A joined connection shutdown task does not establish lower RMCP RunningService, local child, process-group, stderr or HTTP worker completion. Separate lower proposal required.",
    "RetainedTask retains exact task/result, not every capture destroyed by runtime abort; lower resources require separate primary owners.",
    "Runtime observes current connection snapshot only; lower generations/partial initialization require separate roster custody.",
    "If managed cleanup loses ThreadManagerState, global task registry retains outcome but current host report cannot aggregate it. Process-wide MCP ownership admission and final aggregation remain incomplete.",
    "Snapshot shutdown does not fence every new thread admission; process-final admission/aggregate audit remains separate.",
    "No real embedded A-to-B, installed slow-store46s, rebuilt held-host or GUI cleanup gate run for this candidate.",
    "Pinned RMCP HTTP worker logical result is inaccessible through current public API; lower proposal must classify Unconfirmed rather than clean.",
    "New internal session failure receipt field requires separately reviewed acceptance-parser binding before using fixture with this upper stage."
  ],
  "review_units_rationale": "Atomic exact-task custody plus non-discarding error propagation spans these six conceptual review units; validate combined. Do not present publication splitting as independent test proof."
